(1175849, 145583, 27847, '<td valign="top">Hey let me guess; you got ''the good'' and ''the evil'' angles on your shoulder and can''t decide which one to believe and trust! Don''t worry we all have those days ;-) I really like this shot, good luck. Oh yeah, dead/hot pixel on the right side of the ear. You can clone that out in a member challenge, FYI.</td>', 'Hey let me guess; you got ''the good'' and ''the evil'' angles on your shoulder and can''t decide which one to believe and trust! Don''t worry we all have those days ;-) I really like this shot, good luck. Oh yeah, dead/hot pixel on the right side of the ear. You can clone that out in a member challenge, FYI.', '2005-02-16 20:23:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1175852, 146221, 23394, '<td valign="top">i don''t know anything about portraiture, so i''m using your image as a guinnea pig as to what i think i would or wouldn''t do in this situation, as well as what i notice and get out of your image.<br/> <br/>i think one of toughest aspects of portraiture is to capture the essence of an individual, without unnecessary props.  you certainly have done that here!  great job.  the lighting, pose, composition, background, exposure--they all come together to make this image.  good work!</td>', 'i don''t know anything about portraiture, so i''m using your image as a guinnea pig as to what i think i would or wouldn''t do in this situation, as well as what i notice and get out of your image. i think one of toughest aspects of portraiture is to capture the essence of an individual, without unnecessary props.  you certainly have done that here!  great job.  the lighting, pose, composition, background, exposure--they all come together to make this image.  good work!', '2005-02-16 20:24:24.000000', NULL, 1),
