(1175867, 146757, 23394, '<td valign="top">i don''t know anything about portraiture, so i''m using your image as a guinnea pig as to what i think i would or wouldn''t do in this situation, as well as what i notice and get out of your image.<br/> <br/>what a killer expression!  the lighting and focus are tops.  not too keen on the colors, but, then again, this is an image that''s all about you.  i hate it when i''m wrong, but i have to guess lens-baby, as i know of nothing else to produce such a weird area of focus.  well, whatever.  this is a cool shot, and i hope it does well for you.</td>', 'i don''t know anything about portraiture, so i''m using your image as a guinnea pig as to what i think i would or wouldn''t do in this situation, as well as what i notice and get out of your image. what a killer expression!  the lighting and focus are tops.  not too keen on the colors, but, then again, this is an image that''s all about you.  i hate it when i''m wrong, but i have to guess lens-baby, as i know of nothing else to produce such a weird area of focus.  well, whatever.  this is a cool shot, and i hope it does well for you.', '2005-02-16 20:29:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1175869, 146587, 22734, '<td valign="top">Very appealing with great shadow tones that breathe. The accented side lighting adds zest and vigor. The facial expression are sweet and the background adds a good ambience. A very good study. Bumping up.</td>', 'Very appealing with great shadow tones that breathe. The accented side lighting adds zest and vigor. The facial expression are sweet and the background adds a good ambience. A very good study. Bumping up.', '2005-02-16 20:31:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1175875, 146727, 23394, '<td valign="top">i don''t know anything about portraiture, so i''m using your image as a guinnea pig as to what i think i would or wouldn''t do in this situation, as well as what i notice and get out of your image.<br/> <br/>i can completely relate to the quietly enjoying the piano in the dark, and can also appreciate your attempt to capture this aspect of yourself.  i think, though, that it''s just a bit too dark, and that the lit parts act more as distractions than supporting elements.  then again, maybe this is exactly what you wanted.  good luck!</td>', 'i don''t know anything about portraiture, so i''m using your image as a guinnea pig as to what i think i would or wouldn''t do in this situation, as well as what i notice and get out of your image. i can completely relate to the quietly enjoying the piano in the dark, and can also appreciate your attempt to capture this aspect of yourself.  i think, though, that it''s just a bit too dark, and that the lit parts act more as distractions than supporting elements.  then again, maybe this is exactly what you wanted.  good luck!', '2005-02-16 20:32:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1175877, 146046, 27847, '<td valign="top">Great use of selective-desaturation, the redish color (which is considered warm and exciting in the) glasses maybe give an idea about you!?! Over all nice shot.</td>', 'Great use of selective-desaturation, the redish color (which is considered warm and exciting in the) glasses maybe give an idea about you!?! Over all nice shot.', '2005-02-16 20:33:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1175880, 146873, 23394, '<td valign="top">i don''t know anything about portraiture, so i''m using your image as a guinnea pig as to what i think i would or wouldn''t do in this situation, as well as what i notice and get out of your image.<br/> <br/>most interesting effect.  <strike>great job</strike> outstanding job lining up the portrait and the profile.  this would be a novel idea to try outside the constraints of challenge editing rules, especially to try with different colors.   in many ways, you have captured the essence of the individual.  i applaud your inventiveness!  8 from me.<br/> <br/>[returning comment:  this has a really wild thumbnail view!]</td>', 'i don''t know anything about portraiture, so i''m using your image as a guinnea pig as to what i think i would or wouldn''t do in this situation, as well as what i notice and get out of your image. most interesting effect.  great job outstanding job lining up the portrait and the profile.  this would be a novel idea to try outside the constraints of challenge editing rules, especially to try with different colors.   in many ways, you have captured the essence of the individual.  i applaud your inventiveness!  8 from me. [returning comment:  this has a really wild thumbnail view!]', '2005-02-16 20:33:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1175884, 146728, 27847, '<td valign="top">Great work on this one. One way to keep a composition simple is to use negative space and you have done a commendable job of it here. Good Luck</td>', 'Great work on this one. One way to keep a composition simple is to use negative space and you have done a commendable job of it here. Good Luck', '2005-02-16 20:34:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1175886, 145836, 27847, '<td valign="top">To the point and direct, that''s what I''m reading from this photo. Nice lighting also, good luck.</td>', 'To the point and direct, that''s what I''m reading from this photo. Nice lighting also, good luck.', '2005-02-16 20:35:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1175888, 145582, 22734, '<td valign="top">A very cool layout with interesting face angle, a great stare into camera from the 3/4 facial position. The hair plays well to frame the head and then even the shirt participates along with the well matching background. An image to be very proud of. Bumping up.</td>', 'A very cool layout with interesting face angle, a great stare into camera from the 3/4 facial position. The hair plays well to frame the head and then even the shirt participates along with the well matching background. An image to be very proud of. Bumping up.', '2005-02-16 20:35:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1175898, 145789, 27847, '<td valign="top">Excellent composition here (IMO)! Simplicity at it''s best, great use of negative space and it adds because your facing into the photo as if there is something hiding in that white space! I would have burned the shadow out of existence (well out of the photo anyways). Good Luck.</td>', 'Excellent composition here (IMO)! Simplicity at it''s best, great use of negative space and it adds because your facing into the photo as if there is something hiding in that white space! I would have burned the shadow out of existence (well out of the photo anyways). Good Luck.', '2005-02-16 20:38:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1175900, 146757, 22734, '<td valign="top">Funny. The well focus eye radiates that jocular state which then is supported by fist and twirl in mouth. A good tiltle also. Bumping up.</td>', 'Funny. The well focus eye radiates that jocular state which then is supported by fist and twirl in mouth. A good tiltle also. Bumping up.', '2005-02-16 20:39:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1175908, 145440, 27847, '<td valign="top">Self-Portrait of your best features, guess that would be your neck! Lovely composition, not seeing the face I think adds that little extra mystery to the overall shot. Oh, and excellent lighting. Good Luck.</td>', 'Self-Portrait of your best features, guess that would be your neck! Lovely composition, not seeing the face I think adds that little extra mystery to the overall shot. Oh, and excellent lighting. Good Luck.', '2005-02-16 20:41:11.000000', NULL, 1),
