(1176913, 146555, 27767, '<td valign="top">Composition: 7<br/>Technical: 7, I wish the closer face had just a tiny bit more light. Maybe if the amount of light for each pose was reversed it might look cool as well<br/>Appeal: 9, Great creativity :)  Love the motion blur of the passing vehicles<br/>Challenge: 9<br/>Overall Calculated Average Score: 8</td>', 'Composition: 7Technical: 7, I wish the closer face had just a tiny bit more light. Maybe if the amount of light for each pose was reversed it might look cool as wellAppeal: 9, Great creativity :)  Love the motion blur of the passing vehiclesChallenge: 9Overall Calculated Average Score: 8', '2005-02-17 04:39:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1176915, 145653, 23394, '<td valign="top">i don''t know anything about portraiture, so i''m using your image to try to figure out what i think i would or wouldn''t do in this situation, as well as what i notice and get out of your image.<br/> <br/>my initial reaction is that i am grabbed by your eye, but as it is looking off-frame, it also leads my view off.  as i come back to the image, i find great work around your eye, cheek, nose, and mouth, but as i move from there, something starts to feel unbalanced.  the lighting on the hand again leads my eye out of the frame.  then i notice how the heavy border has a severe contrast with the other darker areas of the image.  moving back into the image, the lighting in the background, up behind the hand doesn''t seem normal.  all in all, i feel if this were lit and cropped just a bit differently and if your hand were posed in a less distracting manner, you would have a much stronger image.  but then again, what the hell do i know?  this might be exactly what you wanted it to be.  good luck!</td>', 'i don''t know anything about portraiture, so i''m using your image to try to figure out what i think i would or wouldn''t do in this situation, as well as what i notice and get out of your image. my initial reaction is that i am grabbed by your eye, but as it is looking off-frame, it also leads my view off.  as i come back to the image, i find great work around your eye, cheek, nose, and mouth, but as i move from there, something starts to feel unbalanced.  the lighting on the hand again leads my eye out of the frame.  then i notice how the heavy border has a severe contrast with the other darker areas of the image.  moving back into the image, the lighting in the background, up behind the hand doesn''t seem normal.  all in all, i feel if this were lit and cropped just a bit differently and if your hand were posed in a less distracting manner, you would have a much stronger image.  but then again, what the hell do i know?  this might be exactly what you wanted it to be.  good luck!', '2005-02-17 04:40:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1176917, 146438, 23394, '<td valign="top">i don''t know anything about portraiture, so i''m using your image to try to figure out what i think i would or wouldn''t do in this situation, as well as what i notice and get out of your image.<br/> <br/>great take on the challenge!  love the ''30''s p.i. feel this has.  when i think of portraiture being an effort to capture the essence of an individual, i think this most definitely hits the mark.  great work!  good luck!</td>', 'i don''t know anything about portraiture, so i''m using your image to try to figure out what i think i would or wouldn''t do in this situation, as well as what i notice and get out of your image. great take on the challenge!  love the ''30''s p.i. feel this has.  when i think of portraiture being an effort to capture the essence of an individual, i think this most definitely hits the mark.  great work!  good luck!', '2005-02-17 04:43:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1176922, 146461, 27767, '<td valign="top">Composition: 8, I like that some of your head is cropped out. I think neatly cropping to just include all of your head would only detract from the shot<br/>Technical: 8, Love the DOF that softly blurs all but your face<br/>Appeal: 8, Fun feeling shot<br/>Challenge: 9, Transmits message of title quite well<br/>Overall Calculated Average Score: 8</td>', 'Composition: 8, I like that some of your head is cropped out. I think neatly cropping to just include all of your head would only detract from the shotTechnical: 8, Love the DOF that softly blurs all but your faceAppeal: 8, Fun feeling shotChallenge: 9, Transmits message of title quite wellOverall Calculated Average Score: 8', '2005-02-17 04:45:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1176923, 146461, 23394, '<td valign="top">i don''t know anything about portraiture, so i''m using your image to try to figure out what i think i would or wouldn''t do in this situation, as well as what i notice and get out of your image.<br/> <br/>how much fun you must have had doing this!  as a moment, very well caught.  the soft focus, though, is leaving me grasping for details.  visually, i''m having a hard time reconciling the far right--i can''t get a feel for just what your hair is doing.  i think the lighting is also washing out the range of tonalities and character that might be found in your face.  but, all the same, i like the essence of whimsy that you''ve captured.  good luck!</td>', 'i don''t know anything about portraiture, so i''m using your image to try to figure out what i think i would or wouldn''t do in this situation, as well as what i notice and get out of your image. how much fun you must have had doing this!  as a moment, very well caught.  the soft focus, though, is leaving me grasping for details.  visually, i''m having a hard time reconciling the far right--i can''t get a feel for just what your hair is doing.  i think the lighting is also washing out the range of tonalities and character that might be found in your face.  but, all the same, i like the essence of whimsy that you''ve captured.  good luck!', '2005-02-17 04:48:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1176925, 146871, 23394, '<td valign="top">i don''t know anything about portraiture, so i''m using your image to try to figure out what i think i would or wouldn''t do in this situation, as well as what i notice and get out of your image.<br/> <br/>what a bold, beautiful image.  those eyes are just killer.  to me, this is what i consider a foundation-level image, one that can either stand alone as it is, or be offered up in any number of presentations.   you could crop a 5x7 from your face, and have an equally stunning headshot; in fact, any number of crops could be pulled from this.  excellent work with the lighting, choice of background, and focus.  the expression is perfect, and the triangular composition is well-found.  great job, and good luck!  8 from me.</td>', 'i don''t know anything about portraiture, so i''m using your image to try to figure out what i think i would or wouldn''t do in this situation, as well as what i notice and get out of your image. what a bold, beautiful image.  those eyes are just killer.  to me, this is what i consider a foundation-level image, one that can either stand alone as it is, or be offered up in any number of presentations.   you could crop a 5x7 from your face, and have an equally stunning headshot; in fact, any number of crops could be pulled from this.  excellent work with the lighting, choice of background, and focus.  the expression is perfect, and the triangular composition is well-found.  great job, and good luck!  8 from me.', '2005-02-17 04:56:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1176931, 146576, 23394, '<td valign="top">i don''t know anything about portraiture, so i''m using your image to try to figure out what i think i would or wouldn''t do in this situation, as well as what i notice and get out of your image.<br/> <br/>this image speaks volumes, even without the title.  if the art of portraiture is to capture the essence of a person, i believe you have succeeded.  you seem to see yourself as a smaller part of the world around you, where you would rather capture the mundane and make it interesting than focus on yourself.  this has an almost ok-i-did-what-you-asked-can-we-get-back-to-work-now feel to it.  this is something that is so hard to do, to be able to draw the personality out of anything.  the composition and ranges are great, and the expression is perfect.  this is a nice, solid effort, and i hope it does well for you!</td>', 'i don''t know anything about portraiture, so i''m using your image to try to figure out what i think i would or wouldn''t do in this situation, as well as what i notice and get out of your image. this image speaks volumes, even without the title.  if the art of portraiture is to capture the essence of a person, i believe you have succeeded.  you seem to see yourself as a smaller part of the world around you, where you would rather capture the mundane and make it interesting than focus on yourself.  this has an almost ok-i-did-what-you-asked-can-we-get-back-to-work-now feel to it.  this is something that is so hard to do, to be able to draw the personality out of anything.  the composition and ranges are great, and the expression is perfect.  this is a nice, solid effort, and i hope it does well for you!', '2005-02-17 05:03:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1176941, 146372, 23394, '<td valign="top">i don''t know anything about portraiture, so i''m using your image to try to figure out what i think i would or wouldn''t do in this situation, as well as what i notice and get out of your image.<br/> <br/>while i find your flame to be a bit harsh, it does work nicely with how well you''ve lit and composed the rest of the image.  my eye makes a full circle within the frame, from the flame to your eyes to your ear, then around the collar back to the flame.  the high contrast between you and the background are strong, leaving the range of tonalities in your face to bring out your character.  you really have captured your personal intensity within your eyes.  this is a solid effort.  thanks for sharing!  good luck!</td>', 'i don''t know anything about portraiture, so i''m using your image to try to figure out what i think i would or wouldn''t do in this situation, as well as what i notice and get out of your image. while i find your flame to be a bit harsh, it does work nicely with how well you''ve lit and composed the rest of the image.  my eye makes a full circle within the frame, from the flame to your eyes to your ear, then around the collar back to the flame.  the high contrast between you and the background are strong, leaving the range of tonalities in your face to bring out your character.  you really have captured your personal intensity within your eyes.  this is a solid effort.  thanks for sharing!  good luck!', '2005-02-17 05:08:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1176950, 146735, 23394, '<td valign="top">i don''t know anything about portraiture, so i''m using your image to try to figure out what i think i would or wouldn''t do in this situation, as well as what i notice and get out of your image.<br/> <br/>wow!  this is an amazing image.  the lighting so perfectly brings out the intensity and inquisitiveness in your eyes, and the range of tonalities bring out your character.   you have truly captured the essence of the individual.  8 from me.</td>', 'i don''t know anything about portraiture, so i''m using your image to try to figure out what i think i would or wouldn''t do in this situation, as well as what i notice and get out of your image. wow!  this is an amazing image.  the lighting so perfectly brings out the intensity and inquisitiveness in your eyes, and the range of tonalities bring out your character.   you have truly captured the essence of the individual.  8 from me.', '2005-02-17 05:12:50.000000', NULL, 1),
