(1177604, 145571, 6804, '<td valign="top">Norman Rockwell is the first thing that popped into my head when I saw this. (Before I read the title).  Great tones.  Brilliant work as usual !!!   <br/>Composition is outstanding, detail is crisp, lighting perfect.   Only one idea for improving this one, and I''m not sure if it is much of a big deal.  The lead-line from the easel is drawing my eye down to the watch and pulling attention from your face.  I think by removing the dark watch you could improve the over-all balance.  The introduction of the electronics also gives this a time stamp to what would otherwise be a timeless portrait.   9-1/2</td>', 'Norman Rockwell is the first thing that popped into my head when I saw this. (Before I read the title).  Great tones.  Brilliant work as usual !!!   Composition is outstanding, detail is crisp, lighting perfect.   Only one idea for improving this one, and I''m not sure if it is much of a big deal.  The lead-line from the easel is drawing my eye down to the watch and pulling attention from your face.  I think by removing the dark watch you could improve the over-all balance.  The introduction of the electronics also gives this a time stamp to what would otherwise be a timeless portrait.   9-1/2', '2005-02-17 13:24:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1177609, 146881, 33826, '<td valign="top">Clever!</td>', 'Clever!', '2005-02-17 13:27:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1177620, 145988, 6804, '<td valign="top">Brilliant!!!</td>', 'Brilliant!!!', '2005-02-17 13:35:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1177630, 146587, 12253, '<td valign="top">Very nice pose, light and tones.  It might be worth considering a crop to put the face more off-center.  I think the rightmost part can be cropped almost halfway across towards your ear.  I''m sure this will do well.  Good luck.</td>', 'Very nice pose, light and tones.  It might be worth considering a crop to put the face more off-center.  I think the rightmost part can be cropped almost halfway across towards your ear.  I''m sure this will do well.  Good luck.', '2005-02-17 13:42:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1177636, 146857, 2798, '<td valign="top">Excellent all except for the odd shadow across the top of your forehead - I find this distracting. Also might have been worth considering duotone. You look a little red - sunburnt. 7</td>', 'Excellent all except for the odd shadow across the top of your forehead - I find this distracting. Also might have been worth considering duotone. You look a little red - sunburnt. 7', '2005-02-17 13:44:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1177653, 146873, 19503, '<td valign="top">Really cool illusion, I can see the grain was deliberate, still wish it wasn''t so grainy. Bumping to 7</td>', 'Really cool illusion, I can see the grain was deliberate, still wish it wasn''t so grainy. Bumping to 7', '2005-02-17 13:48:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1177670, 145703, 12253, '<td valign="top">Vivien, right?  You are very photogenic and this is a great shot (as have been the shots for your profile images.)  I like the way you''ve done this high key, and there seems to be a motion/brush stroke texture that I really like here, though I''m can''t exactly tell how it was done.  I like the post, the clarity, but the crop is in-between the extremes, which could make the difference between a good and a really great photo.  I see a number of really interesting crops here.  One is a relatively square crop in the upper right, showing just your eyes and the bridge of your nose (hard to see exactly the shape of the crop here, since I am just using my hands to simulate it).   Another would be to try and find a lower end crop, again moving more towards a square here, which I think works well with the head angle.  You are lucky to have such a beautiful subject to photograph.  I had a lot less to work with ;)  Bumping up.</td>', 'Vivien, right?  You are very photogenic and this is a great shot (as have been the shots for your profile images.)  I like the way you''ve done this high key, and there seems to be a motion/brush stroke texture that I really like here, though I''m can''t exactly tell how it was done.  I like the post, the clarity, but the crop is in-between the extremes, which could make the difference between a good and a really great photo.  I see a number of really interesting crops here.  One is a relatively square crop in the upper right, showing just your eyes and the bridge of your nose (hard to see exactly the shape of the crop here, since I am just using my hands to simulate it).   Another would be to try and find a lower end crop, again moving more towards a square here, which I think works well with the head angle.  You are lucky to have such a beautiful subject to photograph.  I had a lot less to work with ;)  Bumping up.', '2005-02-17 13:53:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1177681, 145571, 19503, '<td valign="top">Good one funky, exellent texture and light on skin-wood-fabric. Don''t think anyone can not spot you now.. lol :) Bumping to 9 :p</td>', 'Good one funky, exellent texture and light on skin-wood-fabric. Don''t think anyone can not spot you now.. lol :) Bumping to 9 :p', '2005-02-17 13:57:40.000000', NULL, 1),
