(1179106, 145749, 15811, '<td valign="top">hrmm...pretty good.  I bet a lot of people are complaining about the blown out section out the window...that''s the first thing that grabbed my eye too.  The eye tends to be drawn to the brightest part of an image.  Really, there''s probably no way to correct the exposure problem other than ...<br/> <br/>underexposing yourself really badly...using a REALLY bright flash hehe...or using multiple images blended together.  So, I guess (on a budget) you''d be limited to finding something else for the background (still using the natural light) or cropping that section out.</td>', 'hrmm...pretty good.  I bet a lot of people are complaining about the blown out section out the window...that''s the first thing that grabbed my eye too.  The eye tends to be drawn to the brightest part of an image.  Really, there''s probably no way to correct the exposure problem other than ... underexposing yourself really badly...using a REALLY bright flash hehe...or using multiple images blended together.  So, I guess (on a budget) you''d be limited to finding something else for the background (still using the natural light) or cropping that section out.', '2005-02-18 01:02:26.000000', NULL, 1),
