(1180971, 146841, 3032, '<td valign="top">Pedro for president! Good pose and lighting. Even some light in the eyes. Great toning.</td>', 'Pedro for president! Good pose and lighting. Even some light in the eyes. Great toning.', '2005-02-18 19:28:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1180974, 146853, 23394, '<td valign="top">i don''t know anything about portraiture, so i''m using your image to try to figure out what i think i would or wouldn''t do in this situation, as well as what i notice and get out of your image.<br/> <br/>nice effort.  these are such hard shots to make.  i''m not quite sure how i would handle the lighting.  this looks a bit too strong from the top, as if it''s washing out a lot of tones and details that could contribute to the character of the image.  while you have a decent contrast with the background, i think the folds that are showing tend to detract.  also, i can''t help but feel that the image would be a bit more dynamic if it wasn''t so centered.  but, then again, what the hell do i know?  i take pictures of bugs and blurry taxis.  good luck, thanks for sharing!</td>', 'i don''t know anything about portraiture, so i''m using your image to try to figure out what i think i would or wouldn''t do in this situation, as well as what i notice and get out of your image. nice effort.  these are such hard shots to make.  i''m not quite sure how i would handle the lighting.  this looks a bit too strong from the top, as if it''s washing out a lot of tones and details that could contribute to the character of the image.  while you have a decent contrast with the background, i think the folds that are showing tend to detract.  also, i can''t help but feel that the image would be a bit more dynamic if it wasn''t so centered.  but, then again, what the hell do i know?  i take pictures of bugs and blurry taxis.  good luck, thanks for sharing!', '2005-02-18 19:29:02.000000', NULL, 1),
