(1182472, 146513, 12253, '<td valign="top">Returning for comment.  Love the lighing, and the wincing glaring look.  The background is a bit distracting here and maybe not the right setting for the foreground "mood".  But it''s an excellent portrait, so on second review, bumping up.  Now one of my top picks (though there are a lot of them up there now)</td>', 'Returning for comment.  Love the lighing, and the wincing glaring look.  The background is a bit distracting here and maybe not the right setting for the foreground "mood".  But it''s an excellent portrait, so on second review, bumping up.  Now one of my top picks (though there are a lot of them up there now)', '2005-02-19 17:23:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1182473, 146516, 25655, '<td valign="top">Any chance you''d switch places with me?<br/>I like the clean feel of this photo. The large spaces, the white walls inside, the white sands outside, the feeling of the sun on my face.<br/>The pose is also a strong point of the image IMO.<br/>I would only change one very little thing here in post-processing.<br/>I would make the shadows from teh windos, the same color as the shadows from the banch.<br/>The two different shades of gray are not really necessary and I find them a bit distracting.<br/>Very nice portrait!<br/></td>', 'Any chance you''d switch places with me?I like the clean feel of this photo. The large spaces, the white walls inside, the white sands outside, the feeling of the sun on my face.The pose is also a strong point of the image IMO.I would only change one very little thing here in post-processing.I would make the shadows from teh windos, the same color as the shadows from the banch.The two different shades of gray are not really necessary and I find them a bit distracting.Very nice portrait!', '2005-02-19 17:23:38.000000', NULL, 1),
